@startuml
left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam ArrowColor #64748B
skinparam actorBorderColor #17324D
skinparam actorFontColor #17324D
skinparam usecase {
 BackgroundColor #EFF6FF
 BorderColor #64748B
 FontColor #17324D
}
skinparam rectangle {
 BorderColor #94A3B8
 FontColor #17324D
}
title Resumefolio | Conditional execution and separate deployment
actor "Authorized run requester" as requester
actor "Target-authorized deployment actor" as deployer
rectangle "Resumefolio | System boundary" {
 usecase "Request supported workflow execution\nUC-D10-RUN" as run [[../04-scenarios-and-models/user-stories-and-scenarios.md#uc-d10-run]]
 usecase "Request an authorized deployment\nUC-D10-DEPLOY" as deploy [[../04-scenarios-and-models/user-stories-and-scenarios.md#uc-d10-deploy]]
}
requester -- run
deployer -- deploy
legend bottom
Sources: YML-D01-D10 and UC-D10 refinements.
These are access contexts, not a new accepted role hierarchy.
A successful run does not itself approve deployment.
Required feasibility, isolation, resource and target-approval gates remain open.
Associations show proposed external interactions, not permission grants.
No include/extend dependency or actor inheritance is asserted.
endlegend
@enduml
